    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. We've been looking closely at the mix design and the binder viscosity. Could you expand a bit more on how the viscosity of the bitumen specifically impacts the crack resistance when dealing with those extreme diurnal temperature swings in the desert? I want to make sure we're not overlooking a chemical or thermal stability issue.",
